## Context

`data/capability_timeline.csv` records Alibaba stage 3 (Browsing / web search)
as `2025-03-07` with source type `release-notes` and note:
> "Qwen-Agent QwQ-32B parallel/multi-step/multi-turn tool-call demo with web
> search; rolled out further via Qwen3 MCP cookbooks 2025-05-01 and
> Qwen-Agent Qwen3-VL image+web search 2025-09-23; Qwen Chat web search
> current — earliest verifiable demo date used"

But `docs/capability-timeline.md` matrix cell shows:
> `absent (no first-party source verifiable at cutoff)`

Found during celebrate sweep after PR #422. Same CSV-vs-prose divergence
pattern that prompted the Mistral stage-1 fix.

## Actions

1. Determine whether `2025-03-07` qualifies as a consumer-product milestone
   under the stage methodology (launch in a public commercial product, not
   just a developer demo). The source type is `release-notes` and the note
   says "demo", which may not meet the threshold.
2. If it qualifies: update the prose matrix cell and add a bibliography entry.
3. If it does not qualify: update the CSV to `absent` with a note explaining
   why the demo date was rejected.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] CSV and prose matrix agree on Alibaba stage-3 (either both show the
      date or both show absent)
- [ ] Rationale for the decision is documented in the CSV note field
- [ ] `make check` passes
